---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Custom-Built Tools"
  description="Internal apps, custom integrations, and smart automations for businesses in Golden, CO and the Front Range. When off-the-shelf software doesn't fit, ZeisWorks builds what does."
  ogTitle="Custom-Built Tools | zeisWorks"
  ogDescription="When the off-the-shelf software doesn't fit, we build the custom tools that do. Internal apps, integrations, and smart automations for Golden and Front Range businesses."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 space-y-16">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-orange uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">03 / Custom Tools</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold text-ink leading-tight">
        Custom-built tools
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-ink-mid text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
        Sometimes the off-the-shelf software doesn't fit. I build the custom tools that do. Internal apps, custom integrations, and smart automations made specifically for your business.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <button
          type="button"
          data-modal="gap-analysis"
          class="bg-navy text-cream text-sm px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg hover:bg-navy/90 transition-colors font-medium inline-block cursor-pointer border-0"
        >
          Get in touch →
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- What's included -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-6">What's included</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4">
        {[
          { title: 'Custom integrations', body: 'Connecting systems that don\'t have native integrations. If two tools need to talk and Zapier can\'t handle the complexity, I build the connector.' },
          { title: 'Internal apps and dashboards', body: 'Simple web apps built for specific internal workflows. Quoting tools, scheduling apps, reporting dashboards, data entry interfaces, built for your team and not a general audience.' },
          { title: 'Intelligent automations', body: 'Automations that handle complex logic: document analysis, lead scoring, content drafting, data extraction from unstructured sources. Real production use cases, not demos.' },
          { title: 'Lead scoring systems', body: 'Custom scoring models that surface the right leads at the right time, connected to your CRM and tuned to your sales motion.' },
          { title: 'Data pipelines and ETL', body: 'Moving data between systems cleanly. Building the transforms that turn raw exports into usable input for your tools.' },
        ].map(item => (
          <li class="flex gap-4 items-start">
            <span class="mt-1.5 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-orange shrink-0"></span>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-ink font-medium">{item.title}.</strong>{' '}
              <span class="text-ink-mid">{item.body}</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Who it's for -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4">Who it's for</h2>
      <p class="text-ink-mid leading-relaxed mb-4">
        This pillar fits businesses with a specific problem that existing software doesn't solve cleanly. You've probably already tried the off-the-shelf option and found it either doesn't do what you need, or it does but with enough overhead that the time savings disappear. Examples:
      </p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        {[
          'A workflow that\'s too specific for any template',
          'Two systems that need to sync but have no integration',
          'A report that requires manual steps to produce every time',
          'A process that involves reading and classifying documents',
          'Data in one format that needs to live in another',
          'A tool your team uses daily that could be 10x faster',
        ].map(situation => (
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-cream-dark bg-cream p-4 text-sm text-ink-mid">{situation}</div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Outcomes -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-4">What outcomes look like</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-ink-mid leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          A property management company needed to evaluate 530 websites manually for a prospecting initiative. The manual version would take weeks. A custom scraping and analysis script ran it overnight and produced a ranked list ready for outreach. The tool cost less than two days of manual labor and can be rerun whenever they need a refresh.
        </p>
        <p>
          Custom-built tools are the differentiation layer. The work that proves ZeisWorks builds, not just packages. When the problem is specific enough that no vendor has built a solution, that's exactly where this pillar lives.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Tech note -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-cream-dark bg-cream p-6">
      <p class="text-xs text-ink-light uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">How it's built</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-mid leading-relaxed">
        Most custom tools are built in Python for backend logic and data work, with lightweight web frontends where needed. Automations run on n8n or Zapier. Everything is documented and handed off so it runs without depending on ZeisWorks.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-navy/20 bg-navy/5 p-8">
      <p class="text-xs text-navy uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Next step</p>
      <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Tell me what you need. I'll figure out if it's buildable.</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-mid mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        Describe the problem or the workflow. I'll come back with a specific plan: what I'd build, how long it takes, what it costs. Free. No commitment until you approve scope.
      </p>
      <button
        type="button"
        data-modal="gap-analysis"
        class="inline-block bg-navy text-cream text-sm px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg font-medium hover:bg-navy/90 transition-colors cursor-pointer border-0"
      >
        Get in touch
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- Back -->
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-light">
      <a href="/operations" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">← Operations</a>
      &nbsp;·&nbsp;
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">Back to home →</a>
    </p>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
